      "chunk_id": "6b97676d-c44e-480a-8d38-54df3d81974c",
      "content": "Travel Booking\n\nEmployees should book business travel at least 14 days before departure when practical. Airfare, hotel, and ground transportation should be booked through the approved travel tool unless an emergency, accessibility need, or customer requirement makes that impractical.\n\nManagers approve travel before booking when the trip is not already listed in the department plan. Travel booked after manager denial is not reimbursable unless the denial is reversed in writing.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002011",
      "document_id": "OPS-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "483a6ce6-f231-4b14-9190-948b5d6cd35b",
      "content": "Vacation Approval Workflow\n\nVacation requests of 1 to 5 business days should be submitted at least 10 business days in advance. Requests longer than 5 business days should be submitted at least 20 business days in advance.\n\nManagers approve vacation based on business coverage, project deadlines, and fairness across the team. Managers should not deny vacation without explaining the business reason.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-002",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "ae3318d9-3093-40eb-bece-b2aa8ade381f",
      "content": "Related Policies\n\nTravel bookings must follow the Operations travel process. Vendor contracts must follow Legal approval rules. Software purchases must follow IT security review rules before reimbursement or procurement approval.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "9a6d1350-41b8-4720-91d4-9052b314fdac",
      "content": "Working Hours\n\nStandard collaboration hours are 10:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. local time from Monday to Thursday. Teams may define additional overlap windows when customer coverage or release coordination requires it.\n\nEmployees should keep calendars accurate and mark focus time when unavailable. Repeated inability to meet team collaboration expectations should be discussed with the employee's manager.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "a72be1bf-5c00-44f0-bc47-135dfa3e3760",
      "content": "Office Expectations\n\nHybrid teams should define collaboration days at least one month in advance. Employees should attend required team planning, onboarding, incident review, and customer workshop sessions in person when asked by their manager.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-003",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    }
